;Returns a persons race talents in HTML-form
;ARG - the person in question

@RACE_INFO(ARG)
#FUNCTIONS
LOCALS '= PRINT_GET_RACE(ARG)
SIF STRLENS(CSTR:ARG:モブ子種族) ;for mobs
	LOCALS '= RACE_TR(strMobOGRaceName:ARG:0)
SELECTCASE LOCALS
	CASE "Human", "Village Girl", "Married Woman"
		LOCALS '= "A featherless biped with broad flat nails.\nSome are from Gensokyo and others from the outside world.\nWhile weaker than Youkai they have the potential to hone their skills in the meager lifespan they are given."
	CASE "Youkai"
		LOCALS '= "Phantoms, ghosts, apparitions, beasts, they are known by many names.\nTheir very nature is aligned with traditional misinterpretations of facts.\nBeing metaphysical concepts, they are difficult to impregnate."
	CASE "Half-human half-phantom"
		LOCALS '= "One whose body consists of two parts - a human part, and a phantom part.\nThey live and die like any other human being, but they have two bodies.\nPossessing a lifespan greater than normal humans, their bodies are slightly colder than others.\nIt is also more difficult for them to conceive."
	CASE "Shikigami (Bakeneko)"
		LOCALS '= "After having lived for ten years a cat\'s tail splits in two.\nThus begins its journey towards becoming a Bakeneko.\nCapable of taking on human form, Bakeneko can often wield powers of necromancy and shamanism.\nTheir human forms are sometimes not perfect, leaving a tail, ears, and a rough tongue unchanged.\nThe transformation also makes it difficult to impregnate them.\nShikigami are servants bound to a master, receiving power as long as they obey them."
	CASE "Bakeneko"
		LOCALS '= "After having lived for ten years a cat\'s tail splits in two.\nThus begins its journey towards becoming a Bakeneko.\nCapable of taking on human form, Bakeneko can often wield powers of necromancy and shamanism.\nTheir human forms are sometimes not perfect, leaving a tail, ears, and a rough tongue unchanged.\nThe transformation also makes it difficult to impregnate them."
	CASE "Shikigami (Kitsune)"
		LOCALS '= "Kitsune are fox Youkai that can take on human form.\nTricksters by nature, they are skillful at deceit.\nA fox at heart, they love fried tofu and are difficult to impregnate by humans.\nShikigami are servants bound to a master, receiving power as long as they obey them.\nBinding a Kitsune is no easy task."
	CASE "Bakegitsune"
		LOCALS '= "Kitsune are fox Youkai that can take on human form.\nTricksters by nature, they are skillful at deceit.\nA fox at heart, they love fried tofu and are difficult to impregnate by humans."
	CASE "Firefly Youkai"
		LOCALS '= "This Youkai was once a firefly burning brightly in the night.\nPossesses the power to control all other insects.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Night Sparrow"
		LOCALS '= "The Night Sparrow Youkai stalks those who walk at night and sings its song, blinding them.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Goddess", "God"
		LOCALS '= "A being of power, but not an absolute one.\nWhen properly worshipped, they are content and will grant generous boons and protection to their believers.\nBut draw their ire and disasters and curses will follow.\nWhile gods in their own right, they are not related to the Myriad Gods.\nTrying to impregnate the self-purifying body of a Goddess takes a miracle.\nSome were human at some point though, so it is not impossible."
	CASE "Yama"
		LOCALS '= "Another name for Enma from Sanskrit."
	CASE "Youkai (Oarfish)"
		LOCALS '= "Envoys from the Dragon Palace.\nCapable of borrowing the power of the Dragon God, they can unleash lighting, thunder, and rainfall.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Kasha"
		LOCALS '= "Youkai from Hell that spirit away the corpses of evildoers on their carts.\nThe corpses are thrown into giant furnaces, feeding the flames of Hell.\nThose cremated this way are forever cursed to remain as vengeful spirits.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Hell Raven"
		LOCALS '= "Raven Youkai born from the darkness of Hell.\nThey have existed in the Hell of Blazing Fires for as long as it\'s been burning.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Satori"
		LOCALS '= @"산에 사는 요괴로, 마음을 읽을 수 있다.\n그들은 의식 그 자체를 들여다보는 데 사용하는 제3의 눈이 몸에 붙어 있다.\n제3의 눈을 감으면 의식에서 %HIMSELF_HERSELF(ARG)%을 봉인한다.\n모든 요괴가 그렇듯, 임신시키기 어렵다."
	CASE "Mouse Youkai"
		LOCALS '= "Tiny in stature but overwhelming in numbers.\nThey have the power to find objects that people are looking for.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Nue"
		LOCALS '= "Legendary beasts not too dissimilar from chimeras.\nTraditionally depicted with the head of a monkey, the body of a raccoon dog, the legs of a tiger, and a snake for a tail.\nThey are spreaders of misfortune and are known to take on many shapes.\nNo one is certain what their original appearance is like, if it even exists.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Demon", "Devil"
		LOCALS '= "Malevolent beings that originate from Makai or Hell.\nOften summoned and bound by a magician.\nThey are more closely related to Youkai than Oni.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Kappa"
		LOCALS '= "An aquatic race of Youkai that can excel in any field that is their passion.\nOften manifesting in the form of great inventions or architecture.\nTheir fickle nature makes them ill-suited for collaboration.\nOften found in rivers, they are fond of cucumbers and wrestling.\nThey also steal people\'s souls by pulling it out of their asses.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Moon Rabbit"
		LOCALS '= "달 출신의 인간형 요괴 토끼입니다.\n느긋한 삶을 즐기지만 때로는 전쟁에 동원되기도 합니다.\n주인의 죄를 씻기 위해 떡을 찧습니다.\n다른 요괴와 마찬가지로 임신시키기 어렵습니다."
	CASE "Youkai Rabbit", "Inaba", "Saleswoman"
		LOCALS '= "지상 출신의 인간형 요괴 토끼입니다.\n느긋한 삶을 중요하게 여기며 타고난 마력을 지니고 있습니다.\n보름달을 멀리하기 위해 떡을 찧습니다.\n다른 요괴와 마찬가지로 임신시키기 어렵습니다."
	CASE "Hashihime"
		LOCALS '= "하시히메. 질투와 시기에서 태어난 요괴입니다.\n이름처럼 다리를 「지키며」 건너려는 사람을 괴롭힙니다.\n그들에게 질투받지 않도록 조심하세요.\n다른 요괴와 마찬가지로 임신시키기 어렵습니다."
	CASE "Wolf-woman"
		LOCALS '= "A female wolf-man.\nWhile similar to werewolves, they do not turn into wolves at full moon.\nInstead, they just become very hairy.\nThey also tend to go into heat around that time.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Bake-danuki", "Bakedanuki", "Ibara Tanuki"
		LOCALS '= @"너구리 요괴는 자신(%HIMSELF_HERSELF(ARG)%)뿐만 아니라 아이템도 변형할 수 있다.\n놀란다면 그 능력은 즉시 효력을 잃는다.\n거대한 고환을 가진 것으로 알려져 있다.\n모든 요괴와 마찬가지로, 임신시키기는 어렵다."
	CASE "Inchling"
		LOCALS '= "Tiny Youkai, often around 10-15 centimeters.\nThe most famous Inchling in history is Issun-bōshi, who was found in a bowl in a turnip field.\nIssun-bōshi had a mallet called the Miracle Mallet.\nIt can change the size of any object and grant wishes.\nOnly descendants of Issun-bōshi can use it.\nBeing so small, it is difficult for them to find love with other species.\nThey are remarkably stretchy though.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one.\nIn this case though, the size is the bigger concern."
	CASE "Rokurokubi"
		LOCALS '= "A headless Youkai with many heads.\nIt can detach and create heads at will without any ill side effect.\nThey have a tendency to lose their body at times.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Tsurube-otoshi"
		LOCALS '= "Youkai that hide from above and then drop down upon unsuspecting victims, killing them.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Tsuchigumo"
		LOCALS '= "Dirt Spider - Youkai capable of firing spider-like webs.\nThe “dirt” comes from them being riddled with diseases and being carriers of death.\nCapable of manipulating diseases, they sometimes lose control and spread terrible plagues.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Youkai (Formerly Human)"
		LOCALS '= "To maintain Gensokyo the way it is for the benefit of everyone, an ironclad rule was laid down.\nTransforming from human to youkai is the greatest sin one can commit.\nAt times, that rule is broken.\nAt times, that rule is conveniently forgotten."
	CASE "Ship Phantom"
		LOCALS '= "Ghosts of those who have drowned at sea.\nThey haunt ships and use their ladles to sink them.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Yamabiko"
		LOCALS '= "An echo Youkai.\nOften living in mountains, they echo back sounds they hear.\nSuch is their skill that they can echo back any sound.\nSometimes they rip a terrible and long scream that carries for immeasurable distances.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Mermaid"
		LOCALS '= "A youkai with the lower part of a fish and the upper part of a human.\nSome aspects of their human half still reveal their fish ancestry.\nHas a lot of difficulty getting around on land.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Amanojaku"
		LOCALS '= @"세상과 어긋날수록 %HIMSELF_HERSELF(ARG)%을 더 편안하게 여기는 요괴.\n슬픔에서 기쁨을, 행복에서 분노를, 고독에서 동료애를 느낀다.\n모든 것을 뒤집어 놓는 힘을 지닌 이들은 누구에게나 미움을 받는다.\n모든 요괴가 그렇듯, 이들을 임신시키기는 어렵다."
	CASE "Makai Resident"
		LOCALS '= "A resident of Makai, thus clearly not a human.\nThere is no real classification for them.\nBut as they are from Makai, they\'re classified as demons.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Witch (Makai Resident)"
		LOCALS '= "A witch living in Makai.\nNeither a human nor a demon, they classify as Youkai.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Baku"
		LOCALS '= @"꿈의 세계에 존재하는 규제 요괴다.\n그들은 꿈을 조종하고, 창조하며, 먹을 수 있는 힘을 가지고 있다.\n주로 악몽을 소비하지만, 때로는 좋은 꿈도 소비한다.\n꿈은 %HIMSELF_HERSELF(ARG)% 분홍빛의 알맹이 같은 물체처럼 보이며 인간에게는 맛이 없다.\n모든 요괴와 마찬가지로, 임신시키기는 어렵다."
	CASE "Yamanba"
		LOCALS '= "Female Youkai that were once humans but were corrupted into their current form.\nThey prefer solitude within the mountains and only deal with other Youkai when they require something from them.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Komainu"
		LOCALS '= "Guardian dogs.\nThey watch over places of worship with stonelike vigilance.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Human?", "Human (?)"
		LOCALS '= "Breathes, thinks, acts, lives, looks, and talks like a human.\nThis anomaly has been classified as a Youkai.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Secret God"
		LOCALS '= "Called the God of the Ultimate Secret at times.\nNo one is sure which secret that is though.\nNot one of the Myriad Gods, nor a Goddess, it is a mystery why it\'s even called a God in the first place.\nThus, it\'s been classified as a Youkai.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Pestilence God"
		LOCALS '= "A God of pestilence, bringing ruination to all that comes near it.\nNot an actual god.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Poverty God"
		LOCALS '= "A god of misfortune, bringing misfortune to all that comes near it, even itself.\nNot an actual god.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Divine Spirit"
		LOCALS '= "The spirit of a human that has achieved godhood, during or after life.\nWhile gods, they are not related to the Myriad Gods.\nWhile Goddesses are still in some form human, these have thrown that away.\nIt requires a miracle to impregnate one."
	CASE "Shinigami"
		LOCALS '= "Youkai in charge of ferrying souls across the Sanzu river.\nEmployed by the Yama, they serve many purposes.\nActing as guides, recording court proceedings, transcribing the lives of mortals etc.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one.\nThe time it takes to cross the Sanzu river depends on them.\nThus, they have the ability to control distance.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Goddess of Autumn Leaves"
		LOCALS '= "A goddess in charge of turning over the leaves for the autumn season.\nOne of the Myriad Gods.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Harvest Goddess"
		LOCALS '= "A Goddess bringing the boon of great harvest to mortals.\nBut only for autumnal crops.\nOne of the Myriad Gods.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Misfortune Goddess"
		LOCALS '= "A Goddess of Misfortune.\nTakes misfortune from mortals and gives it to the other gods.\nOne of the Myriad Gods.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Yaoyorozu no Kami"
		LOCALS '= "The epitome of the Myriad Gods, it's a being that consists purely of faith.\nAs they are born from human belief, they share some similarities to youkai, and sometimes have been referred as such.\nHowever, the two are significantly different, instead they seek out faith, typically in the form of worship.\nThey may split their spirits and manifest wherever called upon, thus enabling them to be in many places at once to serve their worshipers.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Demon"
		LOCALS '= "Like demons, but heil from heaven, with benevolent motivations.\nOften summoned and bound by a magician.\nThey are more closely related to Youkai than Gods.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Fallen Celestial"
		LOCALS '= "A celestial that has been cast out of Heaven for their misdeeds. While losing the majority of their former power, they're still quite formidable.\nSometimes they're allowed back, but the stigma never disappears.\nAs with regular celestials, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Karakasa obake (Tsukumogami)"
		LOCALS '= "A tsukumogami of an old abandoned umbrella.\nTypically portrayed with one eye, a long tongue protruding from an open mouth, and a single foot, generally wearing a geta.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Crow Tengu", "White Wolf Tengu"
		LOCALS '= "Refer to the main description."
	CASE "Hermit?"
		LOCALS '= "A being who poses as a real hermit, or at least tries to.\nWith their origins unknown, what could they possibly hide from us...?\nAs with regular hermits, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Witch"
		LOCALS '= "A natural-born youkai witch. Their power comes from magic, yet their bodies are essentially human.\nSome may even consider them frail, due to lack of exercise and exposure to toxic magical reagents.\nDespite their human-like constitution, it is difficult to impregnate one, perhaps due to magical interference."
	CASE "Magician(formerly Human)"
		LOCALS '= "A human magician turned youkai through their magic research.\nWith no need for food and unable to age, they're essentially immortal.\nDespite their human-like constitution, they're no longer human, making it difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Saint"
		LOCALS '= "A figure canonized as holy in religion, often recognized for their devotion and contributions to their faith.\nOften revered both in Buddhism and Taoism, they're close to being hermit sages.\nUsually ascended to their status after their death, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Menreiki"
		LOCALS '= "A youkai composed of Gigaku masks used for masked drama-dance performances during ancient times.\nAkin to the collective tsukumogami of a mask, they can only possess and express emotions through them, thus their masks are very dear to them.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Avatar of Bishamonten"
		LOCALS '= @"어떤 신들은 극도로 바쁘거나(혹은 게으르며), 직접 나타나기 어렵다.\n그렇기에 그들은 %HIMSELF_HERSELF(ARG)%을 대표할 아바타를 선택하고, 그 대가로 신앙을 모은다.\n신성을 일부 지니고 있기에 임신하기는 어렵다."
	CASE "Wicked Hermit"
		LOCALS '= "Some hermits are labeled 'wicked', often because they break the rules or get too selfish.\nHaving no moral principles and no qualms about committing evil deeds, one must be very careful around them.\nAs with regular hermits, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Magician (Jizo)"
		LOCALS '= "Once an ordinary object, now a magician youkai after being filled with sufficient magical power.\nIn their current state, they're close to being a golem.\nAn inanimate object originally, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Soul of a Stillborn"
		LOCALS '= "미즈코의 영혼입니다. 태어나지 못했거나 아주 짧은 생을 살고 떠난 아이의 혼을 뜻합니다.\n이런 영혼들은 삼도천 강변의 사이노카와라에서 돌을 쌓으며 지냅니다.\n인간과 비인간의 성질을 함께 지니고 있어 임신이 쉽지 않습니다."
	CASE "Ushi-oni"
		LOCALS '= "A youkai typically depicted as a giant spider with a cow's head and vicious claws.\nAccording to some tales, they carry a baby that turns to stone and weighs down their victims, before attacking them from a nearby body of water.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "God of chickens"
		LOCALS '= "God of all that is chicken.\nBased on Niwatarijin, a god of agriculture, fertility, irrigation and/or safe passage, and at times, they're associated with chickens (niwatori).\nOne of the Myriad Gods.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Jidiao"
		LOCALS '= "A Chinese legendary creature, having the body of a tortoise with the head and tail of a dragon.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Kurokoma"
		LOCALS '= "Black-coated Horse from Kai, a legendary horse said to be owned and cherished by Prince Shoutoku that could fly through the sky.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Taotie"
		LOCALS '= "Ancient Chinese mythological creature known for their extreme gluttony, referred to as one of the 'Four Evil Creatures of the World'.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "A Girl of Snow"
		LOCALS '= "A snow girl, a girl of snow! But she's not made of snow!\nWait, what?!"
	CASE "Lampad"
		LOCALS '= "A nymph of the underworld serving the goddess Hecate.\nThey accompany Hecate on her night-time travels and carry torches which have the power to drive someone to madness."
	CASE "Goddess?"
		LOCALS '= "Perhaps one is not always what they seem...\nIn Larva's case, it's possible that she isn't a butterfly fairy at all, but Tokoyo, god of the everlasting world!\nInsect worship intensifies..."
	CASE "Succubus"
		LOCALS '= "A low-ranking demon infamous for their seduction methods and sexual prowess.\nOften summoned and bound by a magician, but there are cases of ordinary humans becoming corrupted enough to become one.\nUsually appears in dreams to seduce men and extract their essence,\nbut steady employment in the bathhouse seems to offer a much more relaxing lifestyle."
	CASE "Paniel"
		LOCALS '= "A Paniel is an automaton designed to aid humans by PnL Industry, an interstellar corporation.\nBecause of their exceptional performance, durability, and loyalty, everyone in the Outside World wanted to get Paniels, from regular households, military forces, large companies, and even the royalty.\n\n- until an anonymous whistleblower uncovered their secrets.\n\nThe main ingredient of the brain cores was the humans' central nervous system, and the fuel for the Paniels was loaded with psychoactive substances to stabilize their newly formed personalities.\nAfter being exposed, PnL Industry left all of its business behind and ran away to Gensokyo.\nAlthough many of their trade secrets were leaked and properties were lost, PnL Industry managed to survive.\nThey still live by selling what they had left to whom they didn't even consider as customers before.\nPnL Industry is waiting for the right moment to return to the Outside World when everyone would have forgotten about the whole mess."
	CASE "Hussar"
		LOCALS '= "Hussars are engineered soldiers. They fight aggressively and with precision, heal fast, thrive in extreme temperatures, and freely ingest military drugs. They have a genetic dependence on the drug go-juice, which also makes them less likely to rebel against their commanders.\nWhile hussars' emotions make them dangerous in combat, they can't relate to baseliner humans. They are famous for their blood-red eyes and \"hussar stare\", a dead expression that unsettles many people.\nTheir lack of expression and burning aggressive nature has led to many violent misunderstandings.\nIn most societies where they live, hussars are kept separated from the rest of the population. Hussars are single-purpose tools - and they generally aren't bothered by the fact."
	CASE "Angel"
		LOCALS '= "A spiritual being in Abrahamic religions.\nThey serve God, usually as messengers, but can also serve as guides and guardians to humans.\nDue to their inherent holiness, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Maneki-neko"
		LOCALS '= "A type of cat youkai capable of attracting money and customers to a place of business.\nThey usually have white fur, but can be calico cats as well.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Yamajorou"
		LOCALS '= "A more sociable subspecies of Yamanba.\nThey are often found running gambling dens, brothels, and other houses of ill repute.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Kuda-gitsune"
		LOCALS '= "A type of fox youkai that live in bamboo pipes.\nThey have potent magical powers and can bestow great wealth on their masters, but feed on their masters' vitality in the process, inevitably leading them to ruin.\nTo use them as a familiar, it's required to keep a male/female pair, but as they steadily increase their numbers, they will rapidly consume all its supposed \"master\" possesses.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Great Tengu"
		LOCALS '= "The middle managers of tengu society.\nThey give orders to the lower ranking tengu, and are responsible for ensuring the health and continued prosperity of tengu society.\nSometimes they also give orders to other youkai living in their territory, but as they are not tengu, these youkai are not bound to obey them.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Oomukade"
		LOCALS '= "A giant centipede youkai.\nAn incredibly powerful species of youkai, they're rumored to consume even giant serpents and dragons through their highly potent toxins and exceptional magic power.\nTheir thick skins and sturdy bodies makes it difficult for weapons to penetrate their bodies, but human saliva is highly poisonous to them.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Ascended Oni?"
		LOCALS '= "A Buddha who may or may not be an oni, or even one of the Big Four of the Mountain.\nOne thing is certain, however, and that is that it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Yazata"
		LOCALS '= "A divine being in Zoroastrianism.\nSomewhere between an angel and a god.\nThey personify abstract ideas and virtues, such as justice, or natural forces, such as fire or water.\nDue to their inherent holiness, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Sarugami"
		LOCALS '= "The legendary king of monkeys, able to control wild monkeys.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Tenkajin"
		LOCALS '= "A blood-sucking will-o'-wisp from folklore in what is now the town of Tamamura.\nIt bears a resemblance to the blood-sucking Chupacabra of American folklore.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Yomotsu-shikome"
		LOCALS '= "A female Oni that dwells in Yomi, the land of the dead. Originally depicted as ugly creatures,\nthey're based on the story of a demon-hag sent by the dead Izanami to pursue her husband Izanagi.\nThey drag their victims into the deepest parts of Hell, never letting anyone escape their grasp.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Human oni"
		LOCALS '= "Formerly a human monk who turned into an oni after willingly falling into the depths of Hell.\nSaid to command great admiration and respect from the hell-dwellers through sheer self-confidence, and uses this influence to command a great many oni.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Immortal Yamainu"
		LOCALS '= "Yamainu, literally meaning 「Mountain dog」, but is more commonly known as the Japanese wolf.\nIt's said that once a Yamainu knows of the taste of human flesh, \nit will become forever cursed, and will never in their lifetime be able to turn back to being the leisuring beast it once was again.\nBut with dedication, such Yamainu can still redeem themselves, to become more holy than wicked in time.\nAs with all Youkai, it is difficult to impregnate one."
	CASE "Sagacious Spirit"
		LOCALS '= "A soul that has been purified to such an extent that it has taken on aspects of divinity.\nWhile similar to a Divine Spirit, it is difficult to properly classify them.\nHowever, they do not require worship, and sustain their own existence, much like hermits.\nExisting in a state from before things are named, their nature is defined solely by themselves.\nAs a pristine existence that rejects life and death, it is difficult to impregnate them."
	CASE "Human (Living God)"
		LOCALS '= "A human who has achieved divinity while still alive.\nBeing able to gather faith by themselves, they can perform miracles.\nAs they have yet to abandon their humanity, it is no harder for them to become pregnant than an ordinary human."
